ontent.com/u/1687918?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless","html_url":"https://github.com/Faless","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-02T12:01:17Z","updated_at":"2025-06-02T12:01:17Z","body":"As I mentioned in #107038 ...\r\n\r\nI think it's okay to have all the handler as functions, but using functions pointers like that it's IMO really bad (and if you ask me, should be changed back to if/else).\r\n\r\nIt makes it really hard to know which messages you are parsing in each debugger, hiding everything inside a layer of macros (that also breaks jumping around code).\r\n\r\nYou should be able to tell which messages are being parsed by just looking at the parse function, without having to go through exotic macros that generate functions names.","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2930345231/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]